Root cause:
The bug was caused by a race condition between the initialization and removal of the driver and the interrupt handlers. This race condition could lead to the interrupt handler being invoked while the driver was in the process of being initialized or removed, resulting in undefined behavior and warnings during execution. The patch addresses this by ensuring proper ordering of resource allocation and IRQ registration/unregistration using devres, which helps to manage the lifecycle of these resources more safely.
